      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1f07cd64",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "democrats",
      "label": "Democratic Party",
      "description": "The Democratic Party is one of the two major political parties in the United States. In the context of this meme, it is implicitly referenced as a political entity being blamed for a catastrophic event (the 'near-death' of the baby). This is a direct political attack, using the party as a scapegoat, which is a common tactic in politically charged memes. The meme relies on the viewer's knowledge of U.S. political divisions and the tendency to attribute blame to specific parties for societal problems.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a4741894"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_bb39d627",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "anchor_baby_rhetoric",
      "label": "Anchor Baby Rhetoric",
      "description": "This is a political and social trope that refers to the idea that children born to immigrants in a country (often the U.S.) are 'anchor babies' — meaning they are seen as a way for parents to gain legal residency or citizenship, and sometimes as a burden on the host country. The meme uses the image of a newborn baby to imply that the baby narrowly escaped harm because 'the democrats' didn't kill it — which is a direct reference to the 'anchor baby' rhetoric, which is often used to criticize immigration policies and to suggest that immigrants are taking advantage of the system. This trope is frequently used in anti-immigrant and anti-Democratic rhetoric.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a4741894"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_bfff3e2d",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "political_hate_meme",
      "label": "Political Hate Meme",
      "description": "This refers to a type of internet meme that uses emotionally charged imagery (like a vulnerable infant) to incite hatred or fear toward a specific political group. The meme's intent is to provoke anger or fear by associating the targeted group with a catastrophic event. This is a form of political propaganda that relies on the viewer's knowledge of political discourse and the use of fear-based messaging to manipulate public opinion. The meme is designed to be hateful and is often used to incite hostility toward a political party or ideology.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a4741894"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_387bcd63",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "vulnerability_stereotype",
      "label": "Vulnerability Stereotype",
      "description": "This is a social stereotype that portrays certain groups (often children, the elderly, or the disabled) as inherently vulnerable and in need of protection. The meme uses the image of a sleeping newborn baby to evoke this stereotype, implying that the baby is defenseless and that the only reason it survived is because 'the democrats' didn't kill it. This is a form of infantilization and a way to evoke emotional responses by associating the targeted group with the defenseless. The stereotype is used to make the viewer feel that the baby is a victim of the targeted group's actions.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a4741894"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9cd871d4",
      "@type": "EmotionExpression",
      "instance_name": "relief",
      "label": "relief emotion",
      "description": "The baby's peaceful, sleeping expression conveys a sense of safety and relief, implying that despite a dangerous situation, the infant has survived unharmed. This is juxtaposed with the text to suggest the baby narrowly escaped death, making the calm expression a visual representation of survival and relief.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a4741894"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_157ba4d9",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The baby is mapped as the survivor",
      "description": "The text 'i made it out alive' is mapped onto the newborn baby, implying that the baby is the 'i' (the survivor) who narrowly escaped harm. The visual of the sleeping, peaceful baby is used to represent the survivor who 'made it out alive' due to the intervention or non-action of 'the democrats'. This mapping uses the baby's vulnerability and calm state to symbolize the survivor's relief and narrow escape.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a4741894"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_fa63a320",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the baby as the survivor",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the newborn baby, who is depicted as the survivor ('i made it out alive'). The text 'i made it out alive' and 'the democrats didn't get me' uses the first-person pronoun 'me' to directly address the viewer, implying that the user identifies with the baby as the survivor. This creates a direct semiotic projection where the user sees themselves as the vulnerable subject who narrowly escaped harm due to the non-action or inaction of 'the democrats'. The baby's visual material is central to this projection, as it embodies the vulnerability and relief of survival.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a4741894"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_2b42060a",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Hateful",
      "description": "The meme directly attacks the Democratic Party by implying they are responsible for a dangerous or lethal outcome, using the image of a vulnerable infant to evoke fear and hostility. This is a hateful meme targeting a political group based on protected characteristics (political affiliation).",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_a4741894"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_668cb2eb",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "democrats",
